1
00:00:01,480 --> 00:00:02,480
好了 莉莉
Okay, Lily.

2
00:00:02,540 --> 00:00:04,460
这单子上有你作业要用的东西
I got the list of what you need for your project.

3
00:00:04,460 --> 00:00:06,340
-荧光胶水 -好的
- Uh, glitter glue... - Okay.

4
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:07,186
荧光圆片
glitter dots...

5
00:00:07,186 --> 00:00:10,020
荧光纸
glitter...paper.

6
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:13,200
丹尼尔斯太太说我的作业有太多荧光了
Mrs. Daniels says my projects have too much glitter.

7
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:15,420
好吧 她需要一个丹尼尔斯先生
Okay, well, she needs a Mr. Daniels,

8
00:00:15,420 --> 00:00:17,477
因为作业再怎么华丽也不为过
because a project can't have too much pizzazz.

9
00:00:17,477 --> 00:00:19,540
这只不过是爱尔兰大饥荒的报告
It's a report on the Potato Famine.

10
00:00:19,540 --> 00:00:21,820
抱歉 难道爱尔兰人的眼泪不会发光吗
I'm -- I'm sorry. Do Irish tears not sparkle?

11
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:23,240
好吧 抱歉
Okay. Okay. Sorry.

12
00:00:24,403 --> 00:00:26,340
朗吉娜 约坦
Longinus, Jotham.

13
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:27,620
你们好啊 来干什么呀
Hi, guys. What's up?

14
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:30,420
没什么 来买点东西
Oh, nothing, just picking up supplies to make signs

15
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:31,520
-做抗议示威的标语 -对
- for the big protest. - Yes.

16
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:33,240
对对对 没错
Oh, right. Right, yes.

17
00:00:33,379 --> 00:00:35,191
是什么抗议示威来着...
Uh, uh, w-- and which big protest is --

18
00:00:35,191 --> 00:00:37,700
去回力球酒吧抗议 还用解释吗
We're picketing the Jai Alai Lounge for obvious reasons.

19
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:38,180
不解释
Obviously.

20
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:39,980
-不解释 -不解释
- Obviously. - Obviously, yes.

21
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:41,177
求解释 大爸
What reasons, Daddy?

22
00:00:41,177 --> 00:00:43,720
约坦 你告诉她吧
Um, well, Jotham, y-you tell her.

23
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:45,600
气得我都不想说了
It makes me so angry, I can't even say it out loud.

24
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:46,340
烦死人了
So upset.

25
00:00:47,509 --> 00:00:49,760
我们只知道回力球酒吧
All we know is the Jai Alai Lounge

26
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:51,900
有国内最好吃的汉堡
has the single best burger in the country...

27
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:52,758
如果不算全宇宙最好吃的话
if not the universe.

28
00:00:52,758 --> 00:00:55,820
-里面有1/4磅安格斯肉眼扒 -是1/3磅
- The Jai Alai Burger is 1/4-pound......Prime Angus, - 1/3.

29
00:00:55,820 --> 00:00:57,740
-新鲜爽脆的生菜 -是牛油生菜
- Uh, fresh, crispy lettuce... - Butter lettuce.

30
00:00:57,740 --> 00:00:59,620
还有从天堂运来的调味酱
a sauce delivered from heaven...

31
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:00,258
肯萨斯市来的
From Kansas city.

32
00:01:00,258 --> 00:01:03,340
夹在刚出炉完美烤制的圆面包中
all on a perfectly toasted, fresh-baked bun.

33
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:04,240
上面还洒了芝麻
With sesame seeds.

34
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:05,820
我都想拿来做我的婚礼蛋糕了
I wanted to have it as our wedding cake.

35
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:06,940
下一个婚礼上用吧
Maybe for your next one.

36
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:09,920
都有谁要去抗议呢
So, who's this "we" that's picketing?

37
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:11,760
每周我们都会有一群人集合起来
Every week, a group of us get together

38
00:01:11,760 --> 00:01:14,840
去抗议那些阻碍同性恋事业发展的人
to protest those who have been holding back the gay cause.

39
00:01:15,020 --> 00:01:16,500
为什么没有邀请我们
Why haven't we ever been invited?

40
00:01:16,620 --> 00:01:18,760
因为你们两个不是那么...
It's just that you're not that...

41
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:19,480
关心政治
political.

42
00:01:19,674 --> 00:01:21,495
就是自从...
Uh, um, you know, ever since...

43
00:01:23,140 --> 00:01:24,740
他知道我看得到吧
He knows I can see, right?

44
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:27,182
我们非常非常关心政治
We are very, very political people.

45
00:01:27,182 --> 00:01:28,726
对啊 我们刚刚还在讨论...
Yes, we were just discussing...

46
00:01:28,726 --> 00:01:31,000
-爱尔兰土豆饥荒呢 -对
- the Potato Famine of Ireland. - Yes.

47
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:32,560
我都四年没吃过土豆了
I haven't had a potato in four years.

48
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:34,100
如果你们真的感兴趣
Well, if you're honestly interested,

49
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:35,400
我们这周六中午会去那边
we'll be out there on Saturday at noon.

50
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:36,138
你们也来吧
You should come join us.

51
00:01:36,138 --> 00:01:37,540
-我们会的 -对 带着铃铛去
- We will. - Yep. With bells.

52
00:01:37,540 --> 00:01:39,580
-对 那只是一种比喻 -天呐
- Yeah. That's just -- that's an expression. - Oh, gosh.

53
00:01:39,580 --> 00:01:42,130
其实是莉莉土豆饥荒的作业要用的
These are for Lily's project on the Potato Famine, actually.

54
00:01:42,130 --> 00:01:43,999
-好吧 再见 -好吧
- Oh, okay. Bye. - Well, all right.

55
00:01:43,999 --> 00:01:44,897
-回见 伙计们 -再见
- See ya, Guys. - Bye.

56
00:01:44,897 --> 00:01:45,763
周六见 伙计们
See ya Saturday, guys.

57
00:01:45,763 --> 00:01:47,100
是啊 很高兴见到你 再见
Yeah, good to see you. Bye.

58
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:48,397
天呐 这你能信吗
Oh, my god. Can you believe that?

59
00:01:48,397 --> 00:01:49,320
对啊 对于一个
Yeah, he's a little hippy

60
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:50,840
不吃土豆的人来说 他也太嬉皮了吧
for somebody that doesn't eat potatoes.

61
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:08,900
就在艾丽克斯毕业一周前
We were called into Principal Brown's office

62
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:10,960
我们被请到布朗校长的办公室
one week before Alex's graduation.

63
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:12,780
这只有两种可能
That can mean only one of two things.

64
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:14,540
要么艾丽克斯要做学生代表致告别辞
Either she's gonna be valedictorian

65
00:02:14,540 --> 00:02:16,880
要么他们要给最性感爸爸颁奖了
or they're giving an award for sexiest dad.

66
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:19,520
我们为艾丽克斯感到骄傲
We're very proud of Alex.

67
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:21,360
亲爱的
Honey.

68
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:23,260
抱歉
I'm sorry.

69
00:02:23,620 --> 00:02:24,680
我只是觉得我这辈子的努力
I just feel like my whole life

70
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:25,700
一直都是为了这一刻
has been building up to this point.

71
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:26,317
我知道
I know.

72
00:02:26,317 --> 00:02:27,968
你们好啊 邓菲们
Hello, Dunphys.

73
00:02:28,460 --> 00:02:29,620
能在繁多的会面中
So nice to be able to

74
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:31,340
告诉你们一则好消息 真是太好了
give you some good news in one of these meetings.

75
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:32,720
顺便问一句 海莉好吗
How is Haley, by the way?

76
00:02:33,021 --> 00:02:35,047
很抱歉我们迟到了 我们
So sorry we're late. We --

77
00:02:35,759 --> 00:02:37,140
-她来这里干什么 -他来这里干什么
- What's she doing here? - What's he doing here?

78
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:39,040
艾丽克斯和桑杰
Well, Alex and Sanjay,

79
00:02:39,240 --> 00:02:41,660
在四年的激烈竞争之后
after four years of spirited competition,

80
00:02:41,660 --> 00:02:43,100
我很高兴地告诉你们
I am very pleased to tell you

81
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:46,900
你们两个将成为巴利高中2015届的
that you are the Pali High class of 2015 --

82
00:02:48,085 --> 00:02:49,565
联合学生代表
co-valedictorians!

83
00:02:49,565 --> 00:02:51,500
太棒了 太棒了
That's amazing! Yes!

84
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:54,198
太为你们感到骄傲了
Couldn't be more proud of the both of you, huh?

85
00:02:54,198 --> 00:02:55,600
你说联合学生代表是什么意思
What do you mean -- co-valedictorians?

86
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:57,400
"联合"是拉丁语前缀表意"一起"
"Co" is the latin prefix for "together."

87
00:02:57,586 --> 00:03:00,042
但说真的 联合学生代表是什么意思
But really, what do you mean -- co-valedictorians?

88
00:03:00,042 --> 00:03:03,360
我料到可能会碰到一些令我紧张的质问
Well, I thought there might be some aggressive questions

89
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:06,440
所以我把我的回答提前写下来了
that, uh, made me nervous, and so I wrote down my remarks.

90
00:03:08,020 --> 00:03:10,360
不 我不是要毁掉你们的人生
No, I'm not trying to ruin your lives.

91
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:12,840
只是因为你们两个的绩点持平
It's just that your GPAs are tied

92
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:14,930
小数点后一千位也是一样的
to the thousandth of a decimal point.

93
00:03:14,930 --> 00:03:17,778
-但我的绩点是4.645923 -我的绩点是4.645923
- But my GPA'S 4.645923. - My GPA's 4.645923.

94
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:19,326
她法语期末考只得了个A-
She got an "A-" On the French final.

95
00:03:19,326 --> 00:03:22,169
他的一篇英语论文只得了A-
He got an "A-" on an English paper.

96
00:03:22,640 --> 00:03:23,040
不
No.

97
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:24,000
这简直是噩梦
This is a nightmare.

98
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:25,140
这辈子最糟糕的一天
Worst day of my life.

99
00:03:25,140 --> 00:03:26,879
各位 我们该庆祝一番
Guys, we should be celebrating.

100
00:03:26,879 --> 00:03:28,760
这是真正意义上的双赢
This is literally a win/win.

101
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:30,460
我这辈子这么努力可不是为了平局
I didn't work my whole life for a tie.

102
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:34,040
无意冒犯 校长 但你是学教育学的
No offense, Principal Brown, but you were a teaching major.

103
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:35,680
我想自己核算一下绩点
I'd like to check the GPAs myself.

104
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:36,680
请便
Have at it.

105
00:03:37,340 --> 00:03:38,938
这俩人怎么了啊
What is it with these two?

106
00:03:38,938 --> 00:03:42,198
我同意他们 平局不是美国风格
I agree with them. Ties are un-American.

107
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:44,360
如果超级碗最后平局了 你会高兴吗
Would you be happy if the Super Bowl ended in a tie?

108
00:03:44,700 --> 00:03:46,780
会啊 会有两次夺冠游行
Yes! There'd be twice as many parades!

109
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:49,780
肯定有办法决定
There must be some way to determine

110
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:51,480
最棒的学生是谁
who the best student is.

111
00:03:51,780 --> 00:03:52,640
不幸的是
Well, unfortunately,

112
00:03:52,640 --> 00:03:54,540
所有期末考试和论文都结了
all the final exams and the papers are in.

113
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:55,840
分数已经算完了
Grades are closed.

114
00:03:56,900 --> 00:03:58,840
可不是所有分数哦
Not all the grades.

115
00:04:03,060 --> 00:04:05,200
看来管理员终于修好了我的椅子
Looks like the janitor finally fixed my chair.

116
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:08,060
你们来这里干什么呢
What are you guys all doing here?

117
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:13,580
最后加入联邦的是哪两个州
What are the last two states to be admitted into the union?

118
00:04:13,820 --> 00:04:14,776
阿拉斯加和夏威夷
Alaska and Hawaii.

119
00:04:14,776 --> 00:04:17,300
列举两个内阁职位[橱柜位置]
Name two cabinet-level positions.

120
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:17,920
很简单
That's easy.

121
00:04:18,060 --> 00:04:19,640
上面一层是放杯子的
There's a higher one for the glasses

122
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:21,420
下面一层是放锅碗瓢盆的
and a lower one for the pots and the pans.

123
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:22,760
别骄傲
Hey, don't get cocky.

124
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:24,520
我们开始准备时
When we started studying for this,

125
00:04:24,760 --> 00:04:26,560
你还以为国防部长的工作
you thought the secretary of defense job

126
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:28,343
是保卫"栅栏"
was to guard "da fence."

127
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:31,720
歌洛莉亚要参加公民入籍测试了
Gloria's about to take her citizenship test.

128
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:34,620
这个小跳豆要成为美国人了
This little jumping bean's about to become an American.

129
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:36,560
跳豆是墨西哥的
Jumping beans are Mexican.

130
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:38,560
等你成了美国人就看不出区别了
Once you're an American, you won't see the difference.

131
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:42,240
我给你准备了一份庆祝礼物
I got you a little gift to celebrate.

132
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:44,460
我知道这不算什么
I know it's not much.

133
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:46,180
简直就是什么都不算
It's practically nothing.

134
00:04:46,780 --> 00:04:48,800
这很美式 很有趣
It's America. It's fun.

135
00:04:48,885 --> 00:04:51,640
谢谢 杰 我好激动
Aww, thank you, Jay. I'm so excited.

136
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:54,360
你知道我通过以后就可以担任陪审员了吗
Do you know that once I pass, I can serve on a jury?

137
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:56,820
他们还用电椅 对吧
They still use the electric chair, right?

138
00:04:57,840 --> 00:04:58,440
我们回来了
We're back.

139
00:04:59,380 --> 00:04:59,859
好啊 哈维尔
Hola, Javier.

140
00:04:59,859 --> 00:05:01,960
"带孩子不上班日"怎么样
How was "take your son to not work" day?

141
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:03,360
收音机发明前生活怎么样
How was life before radio?

142
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:07,200
曼尼和我说了你打算
Manny told me about your plans

143
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:09,138
抛弃哥伦比亚之根
to abandon your Colombian roots.

144
00:05:09,138 --> 00:05:12,100
真的吗 就你还有脸跟我聊抛弃
Really? You're gonna lecture me on abandonment?

145
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:13,497
当初你说出门买尿布
You left to buy some diapers,

146
00:05:13,497 --> 00:05:15,340
结果我四年后才看到你
and I saw you four years later.

147
00:05:15,340 --> 00:05:18,440
如果你能像放弃故乡一样忘掉那事就好了
If only you could let that go as easily as your homeland.

148
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:26,880
他们是在吵架还是重新坠入爱河
Are they fighting or falling back in love?

149
00:05:32,385 --> 00:05:33,368
牛
c-cow!

150
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:34,800
牛
Cow?

151
00:05:36,180 --> 00:05:36,740
牛
Cow?!

152
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,660
要抛弃自己国家的女人
The woman who is abandoning her country

153
00:05:38,660 --> 00:05:41,000
连西班牙语的"牛"都不知道怎么说了
cannot remember the Spanish word for cow.

154
00:05:41,012 --> 00:05:42,814
脑子刚没转过来
It slipped my mind.

155
00:05:43,580 --> 00:05:44,020
牛
Vaca.

156
00:05:44,792 --> 00:05:47,345
我办公室外面有个墨西哥玉米卷餐车
There'a taco truck parked outside my office.

157
00:05:50,460 --> 00:05:53,280
看来你俩的体育成绩一样
Well, it looks like you both have the same gym grade,

158
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:55,320
但我发现你们
but I do see here that neither of you

159
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:57,600
都没完成这学期的一英里跑
have completed this semester's mile run.

160
00:05:58,020 --> 00:05:59,260
我们当时在参加辩论比赛
We were at a debate tournament.

161
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:01,438
-我们赢了 多亏了我 -得了吧
- Which we won, thanks to me. - Oh, please.

162
00:06:01,438 --> 00:06:03,440
你对安乐死进行冗长总结时
After your long-winded summation on euthanasia,

163
00:06:03,440 --> 00:06:04,420
人们都想自杀了
people wanted to kill themselves.

164
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:06,940
够了 我们让你们补考
Enough. We will do a makeup race.

165
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:09,300
谁赢了就可以做学生代表
And whoever wins gets to be valedictorian.

166
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:10,240
放马过来吧
You're on.

167
00:06:10,420 --> 00:06:12,980
这太疯狂了 你们如此执念于做第一名
This is crazy. Are we all so obsessed with being number one

168
00:06:12,980 --> 00:06:14,640
搞得我们现在都不能庆祝了
that we can't just celebrate this moment?

169
00:06:14,820 --> 00:06:17,420
是啊 他们不仅高中毕业
Yeah, I mean, it's the end of their senior year.

170
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:18,798
还都进了很棒的大学
They're both into great colleges.

171
00:06:18,798 --> 00:06:21,277
他们该去庆祝 逃学
They should be off celebrating, playing hookey,

172
00:06:21,277 --> 00:06:22,826
去湖边跟朋友的
going up to the lake house to go skinny-dipping

173
00:06:22,826 --> 00:06:24,840
从大学回来的帅哥去裸泳
with their friend's older brother who's home from college.

174
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:26,720
-别说得太具体了 克莱尔 -好吧
- Let's -- let's keep this general, Claire. - Okay. Yeah.

175
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:29,080
重点是 这两个孩子都很棒
The point is these are two amazing kids.

176
00:06:29,080 --> 00:06:30,500
我们该为他们庆祝
We should be celebrating them both.

177
00:06:30,738 --> 00:06:32,940
你这么想我们不感到意外
Mm, we're not surprised you would think that.

178
00:06:32,940 --> 00:06:33,320
很好
Great.

179
00:06:34,220 --> 00:06:34,820
等等 什么
Wait. What?

180
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:36,860
每个家长都想相信
Every parent wants to believe

181
00:06:36,860 --> 00:06:38,560
他们的孩子能和桑杰一较高下
that their child can compete with Sanjay.

182
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:40,440
艾丽克斯的确能和桑杰一较高下
But Alex can compete with Sanjay.

183
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:41,300
不然我们在这里干什么
That's why we're here.

184
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:44,780
桑杰13个月时就会说完整的句子了
Sanjay was forming full sentences at 13 months.

185
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:47,639
艾丽克斯5岁时就在《聚焦》杂志上
Alex had a poem published in Highlights magazine

186
00:06:47,639 --> 00:06:48,900
发表了诗歌
when she was 5 years old.

187
00:06:48,900 --> 00:06:50,240
诗的名字是《绵羊先生买火腿》[相煎何太急]
It was called "Mr. Lamb Buys a Ham."

188
00:06:50,300 --> 00:06:51,580
但其实讲的是大屠杀
But really, it was about the holocaust.

189
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:53,230
桑杰16岁时
When he was 16,

190
00:06:53,230 --> 00:06:56,040
是州里排名第一的国际象棋手
Sanjay was the highest-ranked chess player in the state.

191
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:57,955
艾丽克斯15岁时
When Alex was 15,

192
00:06:57,955 --> 00:06:59,820
她发现了我们报税的一个错误
she discovered a mistake in our taxes.

193
00:06:59,820 --> 00:07:02,120
我们差点少交了好多税
We owed a lot more money than I realized.

194
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:04,400
就艾丽克斯这种背景而言
Yes, we're very impressed with how much Alex

195
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:07,120
她能有这种成就我们也感到很惊讶
has been able to accomplish, given her background.

196
00:07:08,320 --> 00:07:09,740
好吧 你说得没错
You know what? You're right.

197
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:11,780
我们在赛道上了解这件事吧
Let's settle this out on the track.

198
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:13,520
好了 塔克教练
All right, coach Tucker,

199
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:15,420
我们应该可以指望你的公正性吧
I'm assuming we can count on you to officiate.

200
00:07:15,420 --> 00:07:16,680
通常情况下
Well, now, normally,

201
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:18,539
我不喜欢成为人群的焦点
I don't like to be the center of attention.

202
00:07:18,539 --> 00:07:19,620
没关系 我可以找别人
That's fine. I'll get someone else.

203
00:07:19,620 --> 00:07:20,860
我说了我可以
I said I would do it.

204
00:07:20,980 --> 00:07:24,040
艾丽克斯的舅舅是不可能公正裁判的
Alex's uncle cannot possibly be considered an impartial judge.

205
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:25,200
我是体育老师
I'm the gym teacher.

206
00:07:25,260 --> 00:07:27,840
还有谁有能力来作出判断吗
Who else has the training to oversee this?

207
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:29,360
只要有秒表就行了吧
Anyone with a stopwatch?

208
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:31,240
我告诉你 别侮辱我
Okay, you know what? No need to humiliate me.

209
00:07:31,580 --> 00:07:33,160
希望最棒的孩子赢
May the best child win.

210
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:34,700
她会的
Oh, she will.

211
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:37,500
我们定会"刃不血兵"
Consider this moment gauntleted.

212
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:39,120
有这成语吗
Is that a word?

213
00:07:39,580 --> 00:07:40,722
你就装作它是吧
Hold your head up like it is.

214
00:07:40,722 --> 00:07:42,639
只要肯信 万物成真
Vocabulary's mostly a matter of confidence.

215
00:07:48,320 --> 00:07:50,240
很高兴我们能参与进来
I love that we're getting involved.

216
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:50,932
我也是
Yeah, me, too.

217
00:07:50,932 --> 00:07:53,540
我觉得我们的示威标语能够震慑住
I think we're really gonna send a strong message to whomever

218
00:07:53,540 --> 00:07:55,660
任何人 不管他做了什么坏事
to stop doing whatever it is he or she is doing.

219
00:07:55,660 --> 00:07:59,003
"耻辱"也可以震慑住上千种不同的事情
Oh, like "shame" doesn't cover 1,000 different things?

220
00:08:01,580 --> 00:08:03,080
好吧 大家在哪里
Okay. Where is everybody?

221
00:08:04,049 --> 00:08:05,700
基佬的话果然不靠谱
So like the gays to no-show.

222
00:08:05,700 --> 00:08:06,260
是吧
Yeah, right?

223
00:08:06,260 --> 00:08:08,500
是巴尼斯现在打折却没人告诉我们吗
Is there a sale at Barney's that nobody told us about?

224
00:08:09,740 --> 00:08:11,540
-你说真的吗 -我不知道
- Seriously, is there? - I don't know.

225
00:08:12,220 --> 00:08:14,839
朗吉娜和约坦总是这样
Longinus and Jotham do this all the time.

226
00:08:14,839 --> 00:08:16,520
他们靠罪恶感让我们干个什么事
They -- they guilt us into doing something,

227
00:08:16,520 --> 00:08:17,260
结果自己却跑了
and then they bail.

228
00:08:17,460 --> 00:08:19,240
他们在胡娇家的新年史蒂夫派对上也是这样
They did it at Pepper's New Year's Steve party.

229
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:21,140
所有人都要穿成某个著名史蒂夫的样子
Yeah, everybody had to dress as a famous Steve.

230
00:08:21,180 --> 00:08:21,780
史蒂夫·奥斯汀[摔跤手]
Steve Austin.

231
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:22,420
史蒂夫·马丁[演员]
Steve Martin.

232
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:23,240
他们没来
They bailed,

233
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:24,970
我们被困在一屋子桑德海姆里[音乐剧作家]
and we got stuck in a room full of Sondheims.

234
00:08:25,680 --> 00:08:26,760
你怎么样
How are you doing?

235
00:08:26,860 --> 00:08:28,100
我叫史蒂夫
My name is Steve.

236
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:31,260
打扰你下
Hi. Excuse me.

237
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:33,600
-两个人吗 -不 不是的
- Table for two? - No, no. God no.

238
00:08:34,541 --> 00:08:37,400
今天下午你们门口来过抗议者吗
Have there been any protesters out front this afternoon?

239
00:08:37,400 --> 00:08:39,160
那些基佬吗 今天没有
Oh, the gay thing? Not today.

240
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:40,400
想都不用想
Oh, of course.

241
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:41,722
我们忙了一个早上
We rush around all morning --

242
00:08:41,722 --> 00:08:43,580
我连早餐都没吃 结果白费了
I haven't eaten breakfast -- and -- and for nothing.

243
00:08:43,580 --> 00:08:45,720
这里的味道闻起来真棒
And it couldn't smell any better in here.

244
00:08:45,980 --> 00:08:47,080
我们有一张空桌子
We do have a table.

245
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:47,922
不 谢谢
No, thank you.

246
00:08:47,922 --> 00:08:50,510
不行 我们不能仅仅为了食物放弃信念
No, we're not gonna compromise our principles just for...

247
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:53,900
我们可以坐在不靠窗户的位置
We'll take a booth away from the window.

248
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:54,806
后面可以 后面有位置吗
In back. Something in back?

249
00:08:54,806 --> 00:08:56,580
-这边请 -好的
- This way. - Okay.

250
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:02,900
天呐 她还在跑
Oh, my God. She's still going.

251
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:03,640
就是啊
I know.

252
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:05,140
还记得她三年级的时候
Remember how winded she used to get

253
00:09:05,140 --> 00:09:07,160
穿尤利西斯戏服走有多喘吗
hauling around "Ulysses" in the third grade?

254
00:09:07,220 --> 00:09:09,980
她那么不协调居然能跑得如此优雅
She's surprisingly graceful for being so uncoordinated.

255
00:09:10,180 --> 00:09:12,437
就是啊 我想拍她摔倒的搞笑画面
I know. I was hoping to get a funny video of her falling.

256
00:09:12,437 --> 00:09:14,734
我觉得是拍不到了
But I don't think it's gonna happen.

257
00:09:15,300 --> 00:09:18,000
我的歌两分钟前就放完了 我都听到了
My playlist ended two minutes ago. I heard all that.

258
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:20,280
亲爱的 我知道我们以前就这么说过
Honey, I know we were all just saying it before,

259
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:22,060
但你说不定真能赢的
but you could actually win this thing.

260
00:09:22,180 --> 00:09:24,520
我不只是说 我说到做到
I wasn't just saying it. I will win.

261
00:09:24,820 --> 00:09:26,080
没有什么能...
Nothing is going to...

262
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:28,580
终于拍到了
Oh. There it is.

263
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:35,660
发生什么事了
What's going on here?

264
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:37,115
我在做蔬菜肉块汤
I'm making sancocho.

265
00:09:37,115 --> 00:09:40,020
边做还边听着哥伦比亚音乐
Yeah. You got your little Colombian music going, huh?

266
00:09:40,020 --> 00:09:41,300
我知道 很好听
I know. So beautiful.

267
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:42,860
你很在意哈维尔的话 对吧
Javier got to you, didn't he?

268
00:09:43,240 --> 00:09:43,680
没
No.

269
00:09:45,180 --> 00:09:46,200
可能有一点点
Maybe a little bit.

270
00:09:46,260 --> 00:09:48,820
歌洛莉亚 别听他的 把那锅炖松鼠倒了
Gloria, don't listen to him. Get rid of that squirrel stew.

271
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:50,740
我买了些庆祝你
I got a few special things here

272
00:09:50,740 --> 00:09:52,320
成为美国人的东西
to help celebrate you becoming an American.

273
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:54,580
你瞧 神户牛排[日本产]
Look. Kobe steaks.

274
00:09:55,440 --> 00:09:56,100
一瓶威士忌[苏格兰产]
Bottle of scotch.

275
00:09:57,220 --> 00:09:57,640
雪茄[古巴产]
Cigars.

276
00:09:57,960 --> 00:09:59,940
要知道这些都不是美国产的
You know that none of that is made in America.

277
00:10:00,260 --> 00:10:02,139
但是把它们都买下来是美国人做的
Buying them all was the American part.

278
00:10:02,139 --> 00:10:03,813
杰 我没心情
Jay, I'm not in the mood.

279
00:10:03,951 --> 00:10:05,700
-我有些困惑 -好吧
- I am having some doubts. - Okay.

280
00:10:05,700 --> 00:10:07,140
你听了哈维尔的话 现在该听我的了
You listened to Javier. Now listen to me.

281
00:10:07,140 --> 00:10:10,260
你知道我为什么想让你成为美国人吗
Do you know why I want you to become an American citizen?

282
00:10:11,640 --> 00:10:13,120
因为我曾为这个国家战斗过
Because I fought for this country.

283
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:15,400
我父亲也为这国家战斗过
My father fought for this country.

284
00:10:15,639 --> 00:10:19,550
因为这个国度一向坚持自由和平等
Because this country's all about freedom and opportunity,

285
00:10:19,820 --> 00:10:22,380
我希望你能完整地感受这些
And I want you to share in that 100%.

286
00:10:22,823 --> 00:10:24,480
你说得对 那也是我想要的
You're right. I want that, too.

287
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:25,320
抱歉
I'm so sorry.

288
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:26,440
你只是有点怕吧
Hey, you're just a little scared.

289
00:10:26,460 --> 00:10:27,860
我知道什么能让你好过一点
I know what will help you feel better.

290
00:10:28,380 --> 00:10:30,460
我们把牛排一烤 美酒一倒
We'll fire up some steaks, we'll pour a little wine,

291
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:31,680
你把那条热裤一穿
you pop into those short shorts,

292
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:33,040
我在客厅和你追逐打闹
I chase you around the living room --

293
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:33,800
就那事儿 你懂的
that type of thing.

294
00:10:35,900 --> 00:10:36,620
妈妈
Hey, mom.

295
00:10:37,700 --> 00:10:38,800
今晚我朋友比利
Um, I got invited

296
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:40,360
请我去他家吃晚餐
to my friend Billy's house for dinner tonight.

297
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:41,560
别担心 我们不会吃这个的
Don't worry. We're not gonna eat this.

298
00:10:41,680 --> 00:10:42,300
我们吃牛排
We're gonna eat steak.

299
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:43,880
太好了 其实没有比利这个人
Oh, good. There's no Billy.

300
00:10:43,992 --> 00:10:45,680
为什么突然变菜单了
Why the sudden change in menu?

301
00:10:45,680 --> 00:10:48,760
我本来有些困惑 但杰帮我解开了
Well, I was having some doubts, but Jay made me feel better.

302
00:10:48,860 --> 00:10:51,020
他告诉了我他希望我成为美国人的原因
He told me the reason why he wants me to be an American.

303
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:52,860
排队那事啊
Oh, those long lines.

304
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:55,100
-排什么队 -过海关排长队
- What long lines? - The customs line.

305
00:10:55,560 --> 00:10:57,500
杰讨厌每次从卡波回来都要排长队
Oh, Jay hates them when we come back from Cabo.

306
00:10:57,980 --> 00:10:58,380
什么
What?

307
00:10:58,820 --> 00:11:01,700
那个王八蛋想要我背叛我的祖国
That son of a bitch wants me to turn my back on my homeland

308
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:02,960
就为了在机场不排队
for an airport line?

309
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:09,100
我至少得去比利家露个脸
You know, I should at least make an appearance at Billy's.

310
00:11:14,620 --> 00:11:16,100
桑杰 你来这里干什么
Sanjay. What are you doing here?

311
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:17,774
那是什么
What are those?

312
00:11:17,774 --> 00:11:19,053
踝部负重袋
Ankle weights.

313
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:21,140
其实是腕部负重袋
Okay. Wrist weights.

314
00:11:22,260 --> 00:11:23,297
你来干什么
Why are you here?

315
00:11:23,297 --> 00:11:25,480
听着 明天一切就要结束了
Look, uh, tomorrow, it's all gonna be over,

316
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:27,239
入学以来我们为之努力的一切都要结束了
everything we've been working for since we started school.

317
00:11:27,239 --> 00:11:29,400
所以 我想来谢谢你
So, I-I wanted to come by and say thanks.

318
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:30,540
我还不是个医生
I'm not a doctor yet,

319
00:11:30,540 --> 00:11:32,700
但我能看出你的脑子好像出了问题
but it seems like you're having some sort of brain episode.

320
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:35,440
不 我是认真的 谢谢你一直激励我
No, I'm serious. Thank you for pushing me.

321
00:11:35,780 --> 00:11:37,479
你知道一生都追赶你有多难吗
You know how hard it's been to keep up with you my whole life?

322
00:11:37,479 --> 00:11:39,605
多亏了你我才能得到这个绩点
Uh, I have my GPA because of you.

323
00:11:39,760 --> 00:11:41,640
多亏了你我才能被斯坦福录取
I got into Stanford because of you.

324
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:47,220
我得承认我为了超过你
I'll admit I did spend about a few hundred extra hours

325
00:11:47,220 --> 00:11:48,240
确实多花了几百个小时
trying to be better than you.

326
00:11:48,760 --> 00:11:50,040
上大学后我会怀念这一切的
I'm gonna miss this when we go to college.

327
00:11:50,940 --> 00:11:52,780
是啊 我觉得我也会怀念的
Yeah, I guess I'll miss this, too.

328
00:11:52,940 --> 00:11:54,300
我喜欢你
I like you.

329
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:56,342
好吧
Okay.

330
00:11:56,342 --> 00:11:57,120
我说的是那种喜欢
I mean like-like,

331
00:11:57,120 --> 00:11:59,140
像皮埃尔·居里喜欢玛丽·居里一样
like how Pierre Curie liked Marie Curie.

332
00:12:00,816 --> 00:12:02,400
对不起 我说得太过火了
I'm sorry. I-I went too far.

333
00:12:02,400 --> 00:12:04,420
你身上真好闻 我得走了
You smell pretty. I should go.

334
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,640
艾丽克斯去哪儿了 我给她做了奶昔
Where's Alex? I made her a smoothie.

335
00:12:10,380 --> 00:12:11,960
可能原料有点太健康了
Might have made it a little too healthy.

336
00:12:12,620 --> 00:12:14,940
为什么我们只专注于帮艾丽克斯赢
Why are we so focused on helping Alex win

337
00:12:15,220 --> 00:12:17,800
而没有致力于让桑杰输
when we could be working on making Sanjay lose?

338
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:21,060
-继续说 -跑道上有窨井吗
- Talk to me. - Okay, is there a manhole on the track,

339
00:12:21,060 --> 00:12:23,408
因为那对我的计划至关重要
cause it's kind of important to my plan.

340
00:12:23,980 --> 00:12:26,880
好吧 有件奇怪的事 桑杰刚刚来了
Okay, that was weird. Sanjay was just here.

341
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:29,360
他说我们的竞争是他高中时期
He said that the best part of high school

342
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:30,960
最美好的一段 还有...
was our competition, and...

343
00:12:31,580 --> 00:12:32,840
他喜欢我
that he liked me.

344
00:12:32,860 --> 00:12:34,160
甜心
Oh, honey.

345
00:12:36,860 --> 00:12:37,420
怎么了
What?

346
00:12:37,880 --> 00:12:40,420
这个时机选得有些可疑吧
Doesn't the timing seem a little suspicious to you?

347
00:12:40,740 --> 00:12:42,700
也许是 但他看上去很真诚
Maybe, but he seemed really genuine.

348
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:44,660
典型的心理战
Classic psychological warfare.

349
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:46,520
我在精英竞争中见到过
I've dealt with it in elite competitions.

350
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:48,520
我不知道这种事在拉拉队以外也会发生
I didn't realize it happened outside of cheerleading.

351
00:12:48,740 --> 00:12:49,640
仔细想想 亲爱的
Think about it, sweetie.

352
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:52,380
他以前对你说过好听的吗
Has he ever said anything nice to you before?

353
00:12:53,140 --> 00:12:53,700
没有
No.

354
00:12:54,520 --> 00:12:56,560
我亮出幽默上衣的时候都没有
Not even when I break out my fun blazer.

355
00:12:56,880 --> 00:13:00,020
我的天呐 我怎么了
Oh, my god. What is wrong with me?

356
00:13:00,560 --> 00:13:02,220
我不敢相信我居然让他扰乱了我的思绪
I can't believe I let him get in my head.

357
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:04,940
他死定了
Oh, he is going down.

358
00:13:05,380 --> 00:13:08,680
明天起桑杰·帕特尔一生都得屈居第二了
Tomorrow, Sanjay Patel begins a lifetime of second best.

359
00:13:09,060 --> 00:13:10,200
享受你的氢牌饼干[类似奥利奥]
Enjoy your Hydrox cookies

360
